{"path":"\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/' data-target='root' data-title=''>&#8962; <\/a>\r\n\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer' data-target='computer' data-title='Computer'>\r\n\t\t\tComputer\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os' data-target='computer\/os' data-title='OS'>\r\n\t\t\tOS\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os\/windows' data-target='computer\/os\/windows' data-title='Windows'>\r\n\t\t\tWindows\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/network' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/network' data-title='Network'>\r\n\t\t\tNetwork\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n","async":"0","desc":"Rename or delete network profiles in the registry, and stop USB tethering from creating a new profile each connect.","label":"Network profiles","prevArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/windows\/network\/delete_ghost_adapter_names","label":"Ghost adapters","url":"\/computer\/os\/windows\/network\/delete_ghost_adapter_names"},"nextArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/windows\/network\/route_ip","label":"Route IP","url":"\/computer\/os\/windows\/network\/route_ip"},"languageSwitcher":"<div id='language-switcher'>\n<\/div>\n","content":"<div id='message'>\n\t<p>\n\t\thttps:\/\/www.tenforums.com\/tutorials\/28375-change-network-profile-name-windows-10-a.html\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>Secpol.msc &gt; Network List manager policies<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<h2>Rename and delete<\/h2>\n\t<p>\n\t\t<code class='inline'>Secpol<\/code> adds a policy instead of a rename, so the registry is better. No better way to delete and rename.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\NetworkList\\Signatures\\&lt;GUID&gt;<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tLocation:\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\NetworkList\\Profiles<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<h2>USB tethering creates a new profile<\/h2>\n\t<p>\n\t\tUSB tethering creates a new profile each time it is connected.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\thttps:\/\/superuser.com\/a\/877115\/56505\n\t<\/p>\n\t<pre class='indent-c'><code class='block'>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\{4D36E972-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}<\/code><\/pre>\n\t<p>\n\t\tLocate the numbered key like <code class='inline'>0001<\/code> whose <code class='inline'>DriverDesc<\/code> is the RNDIS driver name (shown in Network Connections \u2014 Connect using, and Device Manager).\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tCreate a DWORD (32) named <code class='inline'>*NdisDeviceType<\/code> and set it to <code class='inline'>1<\/code>. Notice the <code class='inline'>*<\/code> at the beginning.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tDisconnect and connect.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tThe computer's network icon will continue to show disconnected.\n\t<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<div id='updated-container'>\r\n\t<div id='updated'>\r\n\t\tUpdated:\r\n\t\t<span id='date'>\r\n\t\t\t2026 Aug 19\t\t<\/span>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div class='center' id='content-body-separator'><\/div>\r\n<div id='sub-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='fb_components'>\r\n\t<div class=\"fb-comments\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/computer\/os\/windows\/network\/network_profiles\"\n  data-numposts=\"50\">\n<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"fb-like\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/computer\/os\/windows\/network\/network_profiles\"\n  data-layout=\"button\"\n  data-action=\"like\"\n  data-size=\"small\"\n  data-show-faces=\"false\"\n  data-share=\"true\">\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='nav-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n\t<a id='nav-menu-prev'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/network\/delete_ghost_adapter_names' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/network\/delete_ghost_adapter_names' data-title='Ghost adapters' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - previous page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div class='arrow'>&#x25C4;<\/div><div>Ghost adapters<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-next'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/network\/route_ip' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/network\/route_ip' data-title='Route IP' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - next page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Route IP<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25BA;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-up' class='XURL item_block_container ' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/network' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/network' data-title='Network'>\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image ' loading='lazy' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg ' alt='Navigation - up level tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Network<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25B2;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t<\/a> <\/div>\r\n"}